72971.body:
At startup ceph-crash ran "ceph -s" without -n, so it authenticated as client.admin rather than as the name(s) later used by post_crash(), and its result was ignored. Under cephadm the crash container only has the client.crash.<id> keyring, so this check always failed with misleading auth errors, while a genuinely broken crash key went unnoticed.

This PR:

- runs the startup check through `auth_names`, in the same order as `post_crash()` (`ceph -n <name> -s`), and stops at the first success;
- if every name fails with an authentication error (rc `EACCES`, or `RADOS permission denied` / `unable to find a keyring` in stderr), logs an error and exits 1, so the service manager restarts it and the problem is visible;
- for any other failure (mon unreachable, no quorum, timeout, no mon address), logs a warning and carries on as before;
- replaces the `timeout 30` wrapper with `subprocess.run(timeout=30)` in both places.

Fixes: https://tracker.ceph.com/issues/81979

